sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/task-containers.md): a task container is never parked. A workspace operation that finds a `ready` container stopped, for example after a host reboot that did not autostart it, starts it again through the resume run. The workflow and step names stay those of docs/cli/task/vm-resume.mmd; the intent carries `runtime: container`.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · a workspace operation wakes the container
  %% kind: task_vm.resume
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane TC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve · Swamp Node
  participant H as Container host<br/>over ssh
  participant TC as Task container<br/>over WireGuard
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>mode converge
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `WakeTaskVmAction`, when a workspace operation finds a `ready` container stopped
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the row is `ready` and records `runtime: container`; a container row is never `parked`, so only the mode `converge` applies
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-resume
  SW->>H: Start the VM<br/>ssh exec · incus start
  %%> How:
  %%> - `incus start` in the container project; a container that runs counts as started
  SW->>H: Wait for the guest agent<br/>ssh exec · incus exec
  %%> How, for a container:
  %%> - a container has no Incus agent, so the step runs `incus exec … systemctl is-system-running --wait` under `timeout 70`; `degraded` passes, the next steps decide
  SW->>TC: Converge SSH access<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 3
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the Swamp Node's authorized key, its TCP 22 rule and `sshd`, as for a `ready` VM
  SW->>TC: Read the guest state<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 2
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `orbit-agent` is active, and the Pi answers with its token
  SW->>SW: Check the guest is ready<br/>assert
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>ready
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>resume_failed, failed step
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the row becomes `failed`; the group asks for assistance, and `task:cancel` releases the container
  end
